{title: There is a Redeemer}
{artist: Keith Green}
{key: D}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]There [A]is a [G]redeem[D]er,
[A]Jesus, God's own [D]son,  [A]
[D]Precious [A]Lamb of [G]God, [D]Messiah,
[G]Ho-[A]ly [D]one,

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Jesus [A]my [G]Redeem[D]er,
[A]Name above all [D]names,  [A]
[D]Precious [A]Lamb of [G]God, [D]Messiah,
[G]Oh, for [A]sinners [D]slain.

{comment: Chorus}
[D]Thank you oh my [G]Fath[D]er,
For [G]giving us your [D]son, [A]
And [D]leav[A]ing [D]your [G]spirit [D]till
The [G]work on [A]earth is [D]done.

[D]When I [A]stand in [G]glory,  [D]
I [A]will see his [D]face,  [A]
[D]There I'll [A]serve my [G]King [E]forever,
[G]In that [A]holy [D]place.
